1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,787
New hires learn on real customers.

2
00:00:02,787 --> 00:00:07,403
Role-play needs senior staff nobody can spare, and one wrong promise can cost a

3
00:00:07,403 --> 00:00:08,280
company dearly.

4
00:00:09,985 --> 00:00:13,731
SkillCoach turns a company's own knowledge into realistic practice

5
00:00:13,731 --> 00:00:16,625
conversations, powered by Gemini 4 on Google Cloud.

6
00:00:17,243 --> 00:00:20,643
An admin uploads product brochures and policies.

7
00:00:22,184 --> 00:00:27,624
Gemini 4 reads those documents and proposes realistic customer types.

8
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:35,528
Every objection and hidden need links back to the passage it came from.

9
00:00:36,109 --> 00:00:38,667
A trainer checks the sources and approves.

10
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:41,469
Only approved customers are used for practice.

11
00:00:43,791 --> 00:00:46,537
Now a new insurance advisor meets Mr.

12
00:00:46,537 --> 00:00:48,319
Tan, a cautious retiree.

13
00:00:48,319 --> 00:00:50,471
His first question is a trap.

14
00:00:53,544 --> 00:00:55,289
Here's the costly mistake:

15
00:00:55,289 --> 00:00:57,301
promising a guaranteed return.

16
00:00:57,301 --> 00:01:02,669
Before it reaches the customer, the Compliance Guard stops it, quotes the words,

17
00:01:02,669 --> 00:01:03,944
and names the rule.

18
00:01:04,295 --> 00:01:06,483
Send it anyway, and trust drops.

19
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,535
The coach suggests a way back.

20
00:01:14,482 --> 00:01:16,962
Pressure selling is flagged inline too.

21
00:01:19,986 --> 00:01:21,610
An honest answer works better.

22
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:26,426
The customer only states facts from the company's documents, with sources on every reply.

23
00:01:35,493 --> 00:01:38,530
Each turn runs a pipeline of Gemini agents:

24
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:43,333
compliance judge, customer, grounding check, trust model, and coach.

25
00:01:45,443 --> 00:01:47,523
Now, the report.

26
00:01:51,228 --> 00:01:54,865
One forbidden promise fails the session, however good the rest was.

27
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:57,308
The overall score cannot go above fifty-nine.

28
00:01:57,668 --> 00:02:03,482
Every score quotes the trainee's own words, verified against the transcript.

29
00:02:03,482 --> 00:02:05,548
No evidence, no high score.

30
00:02:07,636 --> 00:02:10,966
Managers see aggregates, never transcripts:

31
00:02:10,966 --> 00:02:15,148
skill gaps, broken rules, and who is ready to go live.

32
00:02:15,148 --> 00:02:17,316
Sample team data is labeled.

33
00:02:19,387 --> 00:02:21,278
Seven Gemini agent roles:

34
00:02:21,278 --> 00:02:27,634
Gemini 4 Argon for the customer, builder and report, Flash-Lite for the fast checks.

35
00:02:27,634 --> 00:02:29,071
The future of work:

36
00:02:29,071 --> 00:02:32,627
a tireless practice partner for every new hire.

37
00:02:34,227 --> 00:02:35,001
SkillCoach.

38
00:02:35,001 --> 00:02:38,027
Practice the conversation before it counts.
